{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["לחוף ימים — the edge of the sea, where the sea laps and rubs against it. And if you will say: what is the point, since the edge of the sea is very high and one cannot descend there to buy merchandise — therefore he explains:" "והוא לחוף אניות — at the place of the harbor, where the edge is low and the ships come, and the inhabitants of the land come and buy the merchandise that is on the ships." "על צידן — for it is a place of much commerce, as written: ״סוחר צידון עובר ים מלאוך״. And in Isaiah it is written: ״בושי צידון כי אמר ים מעוז הים וגו׳״. And therefore Moshe said: שמח זבולון בצאתך בים לסחורה (Deuteronomy 33:18)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {2 "Supporting verse from Deuteronomy 33:18 supplied as address since Rashbam cites it by 'Moshe said' without a written address; it is a paraphrase not an exact quotation of the Masoretic text there."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:43.764508489Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}